  closing:(s,all,G)=>[
    `At 10:40 he called Tucson. Ray Mendez, his old flight chief, answered on the second ring, the way he had for twenty years, as if he'd been sitting beside the phone, which Sam had long suspected he was.`,
    ((s.picks||{})[10]===1
      ?`<span class="said" data-who="Ray">"Saw you on that Greaves thing,"</span> Ray said. <span class="said" data-who="Ray">"You didn't read the card. I could tell. You've got a face for when you're not reading the card."</span>`
      :(s.picks||{})[10]===2
        ?`<span class="said" data-who="Ray">"Saw that Greaves thing,"</span> Ray said. <span class="said" data-who="Ray">"Some kid from the agency read a card. Where were you?"</span>`
        :`<span class="said" data-who="Ray">"Saw you on that Greaves thing,"</span> Ray said. <span class="said" data-who="Ray">"You looked like a man reading somebody else's card."</span>`),
    `Sam told him about the gas bill. He hadn't told anyone else. He read Ray both numbers and the difference, and Ray was quiet long enough that Sam took the phone away from his ear to see if the call had dropped.`,
    `<span class="said" data-who="Ray" data-tone="Slow, quiet, gruff, careful.">"You tell her?"</span>`,
    ((s.flags.rosylog||G.rosylog)
      ?`<span class="said" data-who="Sam">"I told her we're on track."</span> This time the quiet went on longer. <span class="said" data-who="Ray">"Huh,"</span> Ray said finally, which from Ray was a paragraph. <span class="said" data-who="Ray">"She's your kid. She'll hear it. She heard it when she was thirteen."</span>`
      :(s.picks||{})[11]===1
        ?`<span class="said" data-who="Sam">"Not yet. I'm waiting till I know more."</span> <span class="said" data-who="Ray">"She'll hear that too. Quiet's got a voice, Okafor. She heard it when she was thirteen."</span>`
        :`<span class="said" data-who="Sam">"I told her the odds."</span> <span class="said" data-who="Ray">"Good. She'd have heard it if you didn't. She heard it when she was thirteen."</span>`),
    (s.score>=27
      ?`<span class="said" data-who="Ray">"For what it's worth, you sound like a man who did it right this week. You never sound happy when you do."</span>`
      :`<span class="said" data-who="Ray">"For what it's worth, you sound like a man who'd like a couple of those days back. That's how I know you're paying attention."</span>`),
    `<span class="said" data-who="Ray">"Listen. The jet doesn't care how you feel. You know that. Doesn't mean you don't get to feel it. Means you do the forms right anyway, and then you go feel it in the truck."</span> A pause, and the sound of a screen door in Tucson. <span class="said" data-who="Ray">"Go to bed, Okafor."</span>`,
    `He didn't go to bed.`,
    ((s.picks||{})[9]===0
      ?`Ruth's page was on the refrigerator under the magnet shaped like Colorado, where he'd put it after reading it twice in her driveway with the engine running. <b>SHORT VERSION: EVERYBODY. WRITE THAT DOWN, RUTHIE.</b> He knew about the Petrel the way everybody on a flight line that summer did: the squadron break room TV, three people, June 2035, something in the departure burn. He hadn't known until Saturday that the flight director had a first name a person could call her by.`
      :`Ruth's page had come in Wednesday's mail, in an envelope addressed in green ink with no letter inside. Just the page, and a sticky note: <b>Page one. You'll get the rest one at a time. R.C.</b> It was on the refrigerator now, under the magnet shaped like Colorado. <b>SHORT VERSION: EVERYBODY. WRITE THAT DOWN, RUTHIE.</b> He knew about the Petrel the way everybody on a flight line that summer did: the squadron break room TV, three people, June 2035, something in the departure burn.`),
    ((s.picks||{})[3]===0
      ?`Read my files, Bea had written. All of them. He'd been through the program folders twice. At 11:52 he found the one he'd missed, because it wasn't in the program folders at all. It was on her personal share, sorted to the bottom of the list, the only folder in there named in capitals.`
      :`On Wednesday Quinn had mentioned, in passing, that IT wanted to archive Bea's drive and that there was one folder on it they'd been told not to touch. At 11:52 he found it. It was on her personal share, sorted to the bottom of the list, the only folder in there named in capitals.`),
    `DO NOT CLOSE.`,
    `Inside was one scanned report and a photo of a manila folder with handwriting across the tab.`,
    `<prop type="doc" title="ANOMALY REPORT AR 2207 · HALCYON DEPARTURE STAGE">ITEM: MAIN OXIDIZER ISOLATION VALVE, MOIV-1. ALDERGROVE FLUID SYSTEMS P/N 7740-112, REV F.<br>EVENT: ACCEPTANCE TEST, MON AUG 18 2059, CYCLE 3 OF 5. POSITION INDICATION DISAGREEMENT AT CLOSE COMMAND, DURATION 40 MS. CLOSED INDICATION THEREAFTER.<br>REPRO ATTEMPTS: 2. BOTH NOMINAL.<br>INITIAL CRITICALITY: 1. REVISED CRITICALITY: 2. RATIONALE: SUSPECTED TEST STAND INSTRUMENTATION NOISE. RECOMMENDED BY: SEE REVIEW MINUTES (NOT IN FILE).<br>FLIGHT RULE 2.36 APPLICABILITY: N/A (CRIT 2).<br>DISPOSITION: UNR. UNEXPLAINED, NOT REPEATABLE.<br>CLOSED: FRI SEP 19 2059. APPROVED: B. KOWAL, PROGRAM MANAGER.</prop>`,
    `He knew what the date meant before he checked it, and he checked it anyway. Eleven days before the September 30 schedule review. He'd sat in the back of that review. He remembered it as the one where everything was green.`,
    `Then the photo. Bea's square capitals, the same hand as the sticky note on her monitor, in blue ballpoint across the folder tab. <b>I SIGNED IT. I SHOULDN'T HAVE. SOMEBODY HAS TO OPEN IT AGAIN.</b>`,
    `The rule number meant nothing to him, so he looked it up. ARA Flight Rules, section 2, rule 36: no criticality 1 anomaly may be closed as unexplained without three independent attempts to reproduce it and the flight director's signature. Originator: R. Calder, March 2036. Carried into the ARA book in 2056.`,
    `He looked over at the refrigerator for a while. Then back at the line that said two attempts, and the line above it where somebody had turned a 1 into a 2, and the name at the bottom. Read together they made a sound he'd heard before, the way an engine you've known for years sounds the first morning something's wrong with it.`,
    `Under the fruit bowl the gas bill said minus seventeen. On the screen the report said closed. It was 12:06, Friday now, and the wind had come up off the plains and was working at the back door the way it did, and the neighbor's motion light clicked on for nothing at all.`,
    `Sam left the folder open.`
  ],
